From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-cuda: the prefill's selection Table (tk) carries .logical - the E4M3 prefill token lists were physical and the sparse attention double-mapped them (the loop bug)

PROVENANCE: this line's fix, 2026-11-06, on the marriage port. The
prefill's sparse selection was given tk (no .logical - default false)
so the assembler emitted PHYSICAL page-row values for E4M3, while the
prefill's sparse attention receives t (.logical = c.ls != 0 = true) and
maps token values through the page table: pt[pt[page]] - a double
lookup. Idempotent while pages are allocated in order (pt[p] == p -
which is why the canaries, the decode ladders and every fresh-serve
probe were bit-clean), corrupting the boundary chunk's attention once
pages recycle or interleave (the hardmode battery's --parallel 2 x 104
scenarios): the model mis-attends from the first sparse rows onward and
long thinking generations degenerate into token loops (the battery 75
vs the >= 94 bar; the harness replay reproduces in ~5 minutes). The
decode path was already self-consistent (t on both sides). THE FIX: tk
carries .logical = c.ls != 0 - E4M3 lists stay positions end-to-end
(the design comment's own rule); bf16 (ls == 0) keeps physical page
rows unchanged. OWNER: this line; STATUS: judged by the harness replay
+ the battery re-run.

RE-ANCHORED onto v1.2.3+marriage+pagerows, 2026-11-06: one site in the
tables() helper (was attend only) - v1.2.3 already threads tk into
blockLastRow's indexUpdate and attendLastRow's selectTokensProfile, so
this line covers the MTP prompt-chunk path too (on v1.2.2 it rode t).

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_dsa_block.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_dsa_block.zig
index 4ab08c370..ba0a6b247 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_dsa_block.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_dsa_block.zig
@@ -237,7 +237,7 @@ fn tables(l: Layer, c: Caches) !struct { latent.Table, latent.Table } {
     if (c.ps % (l.lw * 2) != 0) return error.LatentShape; // pages whole latent rows apart (the token lists' unit)
     // an E4M3 cache's sparse lists stay positions (its chunks take each key through the table); BF16's are page rows
     const t: latent.Table = .{ .pt = c.pt, .ps = c.ps, .page_rows = if (c.ls != 0) latent.chunk else c.ps / (l.lw * 2), .logical = c.ls != 0 };
-    return .{ t, .{ .pt = c.pt, .ps = if (c.pks != 0) c.pks else c.ps, .page_rows = t.page_rows } };
+    return .{ t, .{ .pt = c.pt, .ps = if (c.pks != 0) c.pks else c.ps, .page_rows = t.page_rows, .logical = c.ls != 0 } };
 }
 
 fn writeKeys(k: Kernels, stream: cuda.Stream, l: Layer, c: Caches, s: Scratch, rows: usize, pos: u64) !void {
